  "body": "## What does this PR do?\n\nIncreases the default width ratio for the job name column in the Downloads widget so it takes up proportionally more space than data columns like size, speed, and state.\n\n**Before:** `name: 8`, `progress: 4`\n**After:** `name: 16`, `progress: 6`\n\nWith typical visible columns (actions, name, progress, state, time, size, downSpeed), the name column now takes ~38% of table width instead of ~24%, matching the intent of the CSS workaround suggested in the issue.\n\n## Why these values?\n\nThe contributor workaround in the issue used CSS variables of `70` for name vs `10\u201330` for other columns. Doubling `name` to `16` and bumping `progress` to `6` achieves a similar proportional emphasis without any visual changes to the other columns.\n\n## Related issue\n\nCloses #4157\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
